sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, DECISIONS 4 + R1-R4 (process.stop shape: 209, @swamp/ssh, full intent as inputs).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: process:restart
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Target Node<br/>reached over ssh
  CLI->>GW: process:restart 417<br/>--idempotency-key=KEY
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit process:restart 417`
  %%> - syntax: `process:restart <process> [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the numeric Process ID from `process:list`
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  Note over GW: Validate, record the task<br/>Process 417: provisioning · #5130
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to the Node that runs Process 417
  %%> - Process 417 exists and is not being removed
  %%> - the Process can start: it is installed on its Node
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5130 recorded with the full intent: unit or container name, runtime, on-demand flag, Vite plan
  %%> - Process 417 marked provisioning; its desired state does not change yet
  %%> - nothing has happened on the Node yet
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-process-control
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209); every step runs there
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - `kind`: process.restart
  %%> - the Process unit or container name, runtime and on-demand flag
  %%> - the Node's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  %%> - for a production Instance, its release directory
  %%> - for a Vite dev Process, the Vite plan and the Caddy publication for its Route
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5130
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>SW: Resolve check assets<br/>@nckrtl/process-command-assets
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - validates the intent and finds the shipped Process scripts on Node 209
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the scripts check ownership: they act only on the unit or container marked with Process 417
  SW->>N: Make the asset directory<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · mkdir
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - makes a private directory for this run on the Node, under `/tmp`
  SW->>N: Copy check assets<br/>@swamp/ssh copy
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - copies the shipped scripts into that directory
  %%> How:
  %%> - Swamp reaches the Node over SSH from 209 with the official `@swamp/ssh` behavior, the `swamp` role SSH identity and the Node's pinned host keys
  opt production release
    SW->>N: Check the release<br/>check_release.py
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - checks that the admitted release directory exists
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - `process.release_unavailable`; nothing else runs
  end
  opt Vite dev Process
    SW->>N: Publish the dev route<br/>child operation-process-vite
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - suspends traffic to the Instance, writes its Vite environment file and publishes Caddy for its Route
    %%> Shared:
    %%> - `process:create` runs the same child
  end
  SW->>N: Set boot policy<br/>systemctl enable
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - enables the systemd unit, so it starts at boot
  %%> Skipped:
  %%> - for an on-demand Process, which starts on its first request
  %%> - for Docker, which keeps its own restart policy
  SW->>N: Control the Process<br/>systemctl restart <unit>
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - one `restart` of the exact unit, or `docker container restart` for Docker
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the unit or container belongs to Process 417; a foreign one is refused (`process.name_collision`)
  SW->>N: Verify the state<br/>systemctl is-active → active
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - checks once that the Process is running
  %%> Result:
  %%> - this step's output is the projected result: `ready` and the observed state
  opt Vite dev Process
    SW->>N: Check the listener<br/>lifecycle_listener.py
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - checks once that the Vite port listener belongs to this Process
  end
  opt explicit start only
    SW->>N: Mark it awake<br/>install -D <awake marker>
    %%> Skipped for restart:
    %%> - a restart keeps the hibernation wake policy; only `process:start` marks the Instance awake
  end
  SW->>N: Clean up<br/>remove the run directory
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - removes the run directory after a successful run
  %%> On failure:
  %%> - the directory stays, so a resumed run can reuse the scripts
  alt Process active
    N-->>SW: active
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the Process is active
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event and reads the result step once; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record result<br/>Process: active · task succeeded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Process 417 desired state becomes running; its status becomes active
    %%> - task #5130 succeeds with the observed state
  else restart or verify fails
    N--xSW: exit ≠ 0
    %%> When:
    %%> - SSH fails, the unit is missing or foreign, or the state does not match
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code
    Note over GW: Mark the Process failed<br/>task failed · rerun after a fix
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Process 417 is marked failed with the error code; its desired state does not change
    %%> - task #5130 fails
    %%> - there is no rollback; run the same command again after fixing the cause
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5130
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
